---
title: Bananas Foster French Toast with Whipped Cream Cheese
totalTime: 40 min
source.name: Cooking Channel
source.url: http://www.cookingchanneltv.com/recipes/bobby-flay/bananas-foster-french-toast-with-whipped-cream-cheese.html
tags: Breakfast, Alcohol
---

= Preparation =
Leave out @brioche bread{8%slices}(day-old, 1/2-inch-thick) on a wire rack overnight to dry out.

= Whipped cream cheese =
Put the @cream cheese{8%oz}(room temperature), @vanilla extract{1%tsp},
and @orange zest{1/2%tsp}(finely grated) in the bowl of a stand mixer. 
Fit the whip attachment on the mixer and whip until light and fluffy.
Add the @heavy cream{1%cup}(very cold) and whip until soft peaks form.
Cover and refrigerate until ready to use.

= French toast =
Preheat the oven to 300°F.

Whisk together the @granulated sugar{2%tbsp} and @eggs{6}(large) until smooth.
Whisk in the @whole milk{1%cup}, @heavy cream{1/2%cup}, @ground cinnamon{1%tsp},
and @pure vanilla extract{1%tsp} until combined.

Make the French toast in 2 batches.
Heat half of the @butter{4%tbsp}(unsalted, divided) and @oil{4%tbsp}(divided) in a 
#large saute pan{} over medium heat until the butter is melted and the oil begins to shimmer.
Place 4 slices of the brioche bread in the custard mixture and let sit on both sides until soaked through.
Remove with a slotted spatula to allow the excess custard to run off.

Cook until the toast is golden brown on both sides and cooked through, about ~{2%min} per side.

Transfer the French toast to a baking rack set over a baking sheet and keep warm in the oven while you cook the second batch with the remaining butter, oil and bread.
Keep French toast warm until ready to serve.

= Banana foster topping =
Heat the @unsalted butter{4%tbsp} in a large saute pan over high heat until it begins to sizzle.
Whisk in the @light brown sugar{1%cup} and @ground cinnamon{pinch} and cook until the sugar has melted and the mixture has thickened slightly.

Add the @bananas{2}(small, ripe, cut into 1/2" slices) and cook until slightly softened.
Remove from the heat and add the @rum{1/2%cup} and @banana liqueur{2%tbsp}.
Return to the heat and cook until the alcohol has burned off.

= Serving =
Serve 2 slices of toast per person, topped with some of the bananas and their syrup,
a dollop of the whipped cream cheese, some @mixed berries{}(fresh, optional),
and sprinkling of @powdered sugar{}(optional), if using.
Garnish with @mint{1%sprig}(optional).
